  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1234 PM CST Thu Nov 19 2026\n\nA surface low in the northern Gulf will keep a light northeasterly \nflow over the area, keeping our temperatures fairly cool. Moisture \nwill return to the area this weekend, with the return of onshore \nflow, ahead of an approaching cold front. As the front moves through \non Sunday, a low to medium (20-50%) chance of showers and \nthunderstorms returns to the area. Chances will quickly diminish \nbehind the front as dry air moves into the area. It looks like \nanother reinforcing high pressure will move across the area again on \nTuesday, which will keep us cool and dry through the end of the week.\n\nMinor coastal flooding will remain a concern through tonight due to \nnortheasterly flow and long period swell. Inundation of up to 1 ft \nMSL is expected.",
